## What this track is for

This is **Track 2** of the accelerator: *move your agentic system onto Databricks and apply enterprise governance*. You practise on **Wanda**, the guest-support agent of the fictional vacation-rental marketplace {{ s.lab.company }}. Wanda already works. The problem is that nobody can prove it is governed: the model is called with a shared API key, the data is an exported copy, nothing is traced, and quality is checked by reading a few chats.

By the end you will have moved Wanda's **model calls, data access, hosting, traces, evaluation and monitoring** onto Databricks, and, optionally, **trained and served** a model of your own. Then you repeat the same steps on your own agent.

!!! tip "No data preparation needed"
    The lab uses `samples.wanderbricks`, the sample dataset that comes with every Databricks workspace. The lab code is in the [lab files]({{ s.lab.lab_files_url }}), or download it as [one zip](assets/files/{{ s.lab.zip }}).

